Edge-sorter callers: contiguous vertex array (scattered-locals class)

The poly primfuncs build a stack vertex array [x1,y1,x2,y2,x3,y3(,u,v...)] at
[ebp-0x40..] and pass its base to the edge sorter (FUN_0041243c/FUN_00411ebc),
which indexes it as ONE array. Ghidra models the slots as separate locals
(iStack_40..) and passes &iStack_40 -- but gcc lays separate locals out in a
different order, so the sorter reads a SCRAMBLED vertex list (proven live on
L8 frame 0x9b: memory at the passed base = {x1,y3,y2,y1,x3,x2}; a y-value
landed in an x slot -> negative x2 on the unclipped path -> wild span fill
zeroing megabytes of the image, incl. the cdb OT pointer and prim buffers).
Replaces the 5 remaining &iStack_40 sites (sub_410d58, sub_410e44, sub_4114c0,
the +0xe-stride tri, sub_4118d4) with a real int _q[] array, same slot order
as the original stack frame. Sibling sites were already converted earlier.

